//==================================================
// SEP VCS coverage exclusions -- RTL ties in the SEP system logic: the CPU
// wrapper and its alias remaps, reset control, IO/SPI, the watchdog and DMA
// wrappers and their bus bridges, the system peripherals (traffic filters,
// address and ID remaps, output remaps, the system CSR bank with the CPU control
// regblock and the filter and remap register banks, the mailbox), the ROM and
// SRAM memory interfaces, the entropy FIFO, and the ROM, SRAM and eFuse interface
// shims in the reference integration.
// Format Version: 2
//
// Scope: the cocotb VCS elaboration of sep_uvm_top, target `default`.
// TT-owned instances only, plus MODULE-scope entries for the TT-owned modules
// filter_ctrl_reg, output_remap_reg, alias_remap_reg and traffic_filter.
// Vendored tlul_* and el2_mem_if submodules are a scope (.hier) question and
// are not waived here.
//
// Each block waives toggle bits, condition vectors, branch arms or FSM transitions
// that a literal RTL tie, an elaborated parameter, an unconnected DUT port or a
// generate-disabled path fixes on every path into the instance. The annotation
// names the tie (file:line) and the fields that stay graded.
//
// Four rules keep this file honest:
//   * A net that a master, the inbound SoC port, JTAG, an integrator port or
//     software (a sw-writable CSR) can move is NOT listed. Those are stimulus gaps.
//   * A constant that the reference integration (hw/top/sep_ip_integration.sv,
//     hw/top/sep_wrapper.sv) drives into a SEP input port is NOT an RTL tie and
//     is NOT listed. A literal assign inside a module that the reference
//     integration instantiates is an RTL tie of that module.
//   * A bit whose constancy rests only on a logic argument (implication,
//     complement, case default, value set, reset timing) is NOT listed. The
//     response echo fields d_source and d_size are NOT listed.
//   * A bit that any leaf moved is NOT listed. No listed bit toggles in either
//     direction in the merged `all` database; the file passes urg -excl_strict.
//
// Checksums come from `urg -dump full_exclusions tgl` on the merged VDB.
//==================================================

